{"name":"Lavender Haze","hex":"#d3d0dd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lavender","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of European plants, genus, Lavandula, of the mint family.","A pale bluish purple or violet colour, like that of the lavender flower."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Pertaining to LGBT people and rights."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lavender"},{"term":"haze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Very fine solid particles (smoke, dust) or liquid droplets (moisture) suspended in the air, slightly limiting visibility.","A reduction of transparency of a clear gas or liquid."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be or become hazy, or thick with haze."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lavender Haze","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lavender Haze\" is a song by the American singer-songwriter Taylor Swift from her tenth studio album, Midnights (2022). Swift wrote and produced the song with Jack Antonoff, Jahaan Sweet, and Sounwave. Zoë Kravitz and Sam Dew were co-writers, and Braxton Cook was an additional producer. The title was inspired by a phrase used in the series Mad Men that refers to the state of being in love. Republic Records released \"Lavender Haze\" to US pop radio as the album's third single on November 29, 2022."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/af/Taylor_Swift_-_Lavender_Haze.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavender_Haze","wikidata":"Q114801069"},{"title":"Lavandula","blocks":[{"text":"Lavandula is a genus of 47 known species of perennial flowering plants in the sage family, Lamiaceae. It is native to regions of the Iberian Peninsula and Mediterranean coastline, the Middle East, extending to the Indian subcontinent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Single_lavender_flower02.jpg/330px-Single_lavender_flower02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavandula","wikidata":"Q171892"},{"title":"Haze","blocks":[{"text":"Haze is traditionally an atmospheric phenomenon in which dust, smoke, and other dry particulates suspended in air obscure visibility and the clarity of the sky. The World Meteorological Organization manual of codes includes a classification of particulates causing horizontal obscuration into categories of fog, ice fog, steam fog, mist, haze, smoke, volcanic ash, dust, sand, and snow. Sources for particles that cause haze include farming, traffic, industry, windy weather, volcanic activity and wildfires.\nSeen from afar and depending on the direction of view with respect to the Sun, haze may appear brownish or bluish, while mist tends to be bluish grey instead. Whereas haze often is considered a phenomenon occurring in dry air, mist formation is a phenomenon in saturated, humid air. However, haze particles may act as condensation nuclei that leads to the subsequent vapor condensation and formation of mist droplets; such forms of haze are known as \"wet haze\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/MosqueinAbuja.jpg/330px-MosqueinAbuja.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haze","wikidata":"Q643546"},{"title":"Lavender (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lavender is a light shade of purple or violet. It applies particularly to the color of the flower of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Lavandula_fields.jpg/330px-Lavandula_fields.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavender_(color)","wikidata":"Q2468392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Joe_Alwyn_during_an_interview%2C_August_2018.png/500px-Joe_Alwyn_during_an_interview%2C_August_2018.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Joe_Alwyn_during_an_interview%2C_August_2018.png/500px-Joe_Alwyn_during_an_interview%2C_August_2018.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Lavender Haze\" was inspired by the scrutiny on Swift's relationship with Joe Alwyn.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoe_Alwyn_during_an_interview%2C_August_2018.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Taylor_Swift_Eras_Tour_-_Arlington_TX_20230331_-_Lavender_Haze_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Taylor_Swift_Eras_Tour_-_Arlington_TX_20230331_-_Lavender_Haze_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Taylor_Swift_Eras_Tour_-_Arlington_TX_20230331_-_Lavender_Haze_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Taylor_Swift_Eras_Tour_-_Arlington_TX_20230331_-_Lavender_Haze_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Taylor_Swift_Eras_Tour_-_Arlington_TX_20230331_-_Lavender_Haze_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Taylor_Swift_Eras_Tour_-_Arlington_TX_20230331_-_Lavender_Haze_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Swift performing \"Lavender Haze\" on the Eras Tour in 2023","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATaylor_Swift_Eras_Tour_-_Arlington_TX_20230331_-_Lavender_Haze_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c1/Lavender_Haze_%E2%80%93_Taylor_Swift_%28music_video_screenshot%29.png/330px-Lavender_Haze_%E2%80%93_Taylor_Swift_%28music_video_screenshot%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/